  "notes": [
    "The OpenCascade chat JSON is identical after normalising the generated STEP digest, the session journal head and the design-cache flag; the visible text and every design value are identical. The cache flag differs because the Python reference had the design in memory from an earlier call while the Rust run built it cold.",
    "The OpenCascade drawing and section payloads for design 594f408b... are byte-identical between the two front doors.",
    "The OpenCascade STEP files are the same size (55,554 bytes) but their sha256 differs because the OCP STEP header embeds the export timestamp (FILE_NAME ... 2026-10-20T...); the geometry is the same.",
    "The FreeCAD chat is refused by the Rust front door (chat_design.rs finish_design compiles only opencascade); the Python public server builds it. The worker and the Rust /design route both build FreeCAD correctly.",
    "A design restored from the worker journal loses measured.surface_area_mm2 (service.py writes surface_area_mm2 and reads area_mm2), so after the worker restart the UI card shows \"-\" for area on both front doors. The pre-restart card shows 11889.10 mm^2."
